.TH HSH 1 "February 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hsh \- a simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
hsh is a simple UNIX command interpreter. It reads commands from standard input
and executes them.
.PP
It can be used in interactive mode (user types commands) or non-interactive mode
(commands are provided through a pipe or a file).
.SH USAGE
Interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
./hsh
($) /bin/ls
($) /bin/pwd
($) Ctrl+D
.fi
.PP
Non-interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
cat file_with_commands | ./hsh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR wait (2),
.BR getline (3)
